+-- RC4.4: `substituted_at` + `terminalized_at` — expand-only additions to
+-- `reference_call` feeding the §7.6 attempt-log timeline (server-built, AR-RC13).
+--
+--   `terminalized_at` — the terminal INSTANT, stamped by every guarded
+--   terminal writer (complete_reference_call, terminalize_reference_call,
+--   sweep_terminal, exhaust_reference_call, sweep_mark_failed). `updated_at`
+--   is polluted by later writes (a takeover on an unreachable row bumps it),
+--   and `submitted_at`/`objected_at` only cover two of the seven terminal
+--   statuses — the timeline's "Closed — no reply"-style terminal entry needs
+--   a first-class timestamp. The detail read falls back
+--   `terminalized_at → submitted_at → objected_at → updated_at` for rows
+--   terminalized before this migration.
+--
+--   `substituted_at` — stamped on the NEW row by the substitute path
+--   (mark_substituted_reference_call.sql, guarded
+--   `WHERE id = $1 AND substituted_at IS NULL`, inside do_substitute's
+--   transaction). The new row's timeline opens with "Referee substituted";
+--   the prior row keeps its own terminal event. The shared idempotent insert
+--   is untouched.
+--
+-- Expand-only per the repo migration discipline: the previous Cloud Run
+-- revision keeps working against this schema (it simply never reads/writes
+-- the new columns).
+ALTER TABLE reference_call
+  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS substituted_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
+  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS terminalized_at TIMESTAMPTZ;
